<figure class="waste-slope article-wide not-prose" aria-labelledby="waste-slope-title waste-slope-caption">
  <header>
    <p>Failure mechanism</p>
    <h2 id="waste-slope-title">When mixed waste becomes a moving slope</h2>
  </header>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 960 520" role="img" aria-labelledby="waste-slope-svg-title waste-slope-svg-desc">
    <title id="waste-slope-svg-title">Cross-section of a wet waste slope failure</title>
    <desc id="waste-slope-svg-desc">Rain enters a steep mixed-waste mound, raises the leachate level, reduces friction along a curved failure surface and sends material toward houses and a road at the toe.</desc>
    <defs>
      <linearGradient id="waste-fill" x1="0" x2="0" y1="0" y2="1">
        <stop offset="0" stop-color="#7f7052" />
        <stop offset="1" stop-color="#463e31" />
      </linearGradient>
      <linearGradient id="wet-zone" x1="0" x2="0" y1="0" y2="1">
        <stop offset="0" stop-color="#3e92a1" stop-opacity="0.18" />
        <stop offset="1" stop-color="#43bdd0" stop-opacity="0.72" />
      </linearGradient>
      <marker id="arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="4" orient="auto">
        <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 Z" fill="#f08a63" />
      </marker>
      <pattern id="waste-pattern" width="45" height="35" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
        <path d="M3 8h15v8H3zM27 5l9 7-6 9-9-7zM9 26h9m10 2h12" fill="none" stroke="#d2bf91" stroke-opacity="0.32" stroke-width="3" />
      </pattern>
    </defs>

    <path d="M30 438H930" stroke="#7f795f" stroke-width="18" stroke-linecap="round" />
    <path d="M48 420C180 411 248 359 312 244C369 141 450 93 566 114C661 132 714 231 764 343L810 420Z" fill="url(#waste-fill)" stroke="#b49a66" stroke-width="4" />
    <path d="M48 420C180 411 248 359 312 244C369 141 450 93 566 114C661 132 714 231 764 343L810 420Z" fill="url(#waste-pattern)" />
    <path d="M165 398C269 365 305 290 338 229C395 124 504 122 586 167C650 202 689 282 741 390Z" fill="url(#wet-zone)" />
    <path d="M173 402C277 385 326 314 356 246C393 162 476 135 563 162C648 189 695 280 742 393" fill="none" stroke="#f08a63" stroke-width="6" stroke-dasharray="12 9" />

    <g stroke="#77c8df" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round">
      <path d="M370 48l-18 33" />
      <path d="M423 34l-18 33" />
      <path d="M476 48l-18 33" />
      <path d="M529 34l-18 33" />
      <path d="M582 48l-18 33" />
      <path d="M635 34l-18 33" />
    </g>

    <g fill="#d8d3c5" stroke="#191a18" stroke-width="3">
      <path d="M810 371l40-32 40 32v50h-80z" />
      <rect x="830" y="389" width="17" height="32" fill="#222" />
      <path d="M875 390h11v15h-11z" fill="#f2c36d" />
      <path d="M742 407h57" stroke="#f08a63" stroke-width="7" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
    </g>

    <g font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="20" fill="#f4ede0">
      <text x="382" y="26">rain enters the pile</text>
      <text x="432" y="276" fill="#8ee4f2">leachate rises</text>
      <text x="230" y="448" fill="#f3ad8f">curved failure surface</text>
      <text x="741" y="486">road and homes at the toe</text>
      <text x="116" y="118">daily placement</text>
      <text x="116" y="144">adds load and height</text>
    </g>

    <path d="M256 151C293 145 319 151 345 170" fill="none" stroke="#f08a63" stroke-width="5" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
    <path d="M663 229C716 247 751 280 774 319" fill="none" stroke="#f08a63" stroke-width="7" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
  </svg>
  <figcaption id="waste-slope-caption">
    Water is usually the decisive ingredient. In a 62-case study, high leachate levels were the leading coded cause, followed by poor compaction and weak foundations. Fire and gas can interact with the failure, but they are not required.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

